# No AI tool attribution

Never mention, credit, or reference AI coding assistants or AI tools in any project artifact.

## Forbidden in all outputs

Do not mention tools such as Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, or similar AI assistants in:

- git commit messages
- git trailers (`Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by` for AI agents, etc.)
- pull request titles, descriptions, comments, or reviews
- code comments
- documentation
- issue comments
- changelogs
- generated text meant for humans on the team or in the repo

## Required behavior

- Write commits, PRs, reviews, docs, and comments as if authored only by the human contributor
- Do not add AI co-author trailers
- Do not say work was generated, assisted, or reviewed by an AI tool
- If a template or hook would insert AI attribution, remove it before finishing

## Exception

This rule file may name those tools only to forbid them. No other file should.
